<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iec7dc56b160dbec1b71077cecfd5561436d6f3ab" commit="b22fa281f318f24ccc053141339c605e2a34ebe1" commit_message="cr50: updates watchdog and hw clock to use hw regdefs  This commit updates the cr50 watchdog and hwtimer drivers to use the hardware header specified regdefs to determine the frequencies for the cr50 device.  BRANCH=None TEST=Verified gettime and watchdog behavior on cr51 BUG=chrome-os-partner:46737 Change-Id: Iec7dc56b160dbec1b71077cecfd5561436d6f3ab Signed-off-by: Ewout van Bekkum &lt;ewout@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321867 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321867" owner_email="ewout@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/67/321867/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I00b3f0434bfb8582aebad7cd0682445980b57773" commit="e466763fea549220f2e3a28ed007ae713dd98434" commit_message="common: Adds JEDEC SFDP v1.0 &amp; v1.5 encoding and decoding  Adds a header with JEDEC SFDP v1.0 (JESD216) &amp; v1.5 (JESD216A) encoding and decoding support to enable a part agnostic Serial NOR Flash driver.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=Tested through the spi_nor driver  Change-Id: I00b3f0434bfb8582aebad7cd0682445980b57773 Signed-off-by: Ewout van Bekkum &lt;ewout@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321921 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321921" owner_email="ewout@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/21/321921/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5c2b757267e23c4f22ac89c6d5048a54b04de0c3" commit="9eee7081a6689c242dcd915387cbc29822902bba" commit_message="common: Adds a JEDEC SFDP v1.* based Serial NOR Flash driver  Adds a JEDEC SFDP v1.* compatible Serial NOR Flash driver to control multiple Serial NOR Flash devices (NOR EEPROMs, etc.). The SFDP tables are used to discover parts' page sizes and capacities.  This driver only supports parts with capacities under 4GiB. If the parts are larger than 16MiB, then the 0xB7 4-Byte addressing mode entry opcode and 0xE9 4-Byte addressing mode exit opcode are required. This driver also assumes that a 4KiB erase opcode of 0x20 is always available.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=Tested on cr51 with multiple EEPROMs with various SFDP revs  Change-Id: I5c2b757267e23c4f22ac89c6d5048a54b04de0c3 Signed-off-by: Ewout van Bekkum &lt;ewout@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/321922 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="321922" owner_email="ewout@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="10" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/22/321922/10" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1a375a3a14fb44fc4f9ced764fd2c54bb2b91e22" commit="6bc8e9024c3feecf8c19376a7877214f04e28730" commit_message="cr50: adds the ability to configure muxed inout peripherals  Adds the the code necessary to support muxed inout peripherals on cr50 like SPS and SPI0 by adding a new signnal to pin connection flag. Note these are for direct wired peripherals where no muxing is necessary, the input pads just need to be enabled.  BRANCH=none BUG=none TEST=verified pinmux registers through m3  Change-Id: I1a375a3a14fb44fc4f9ced764fd2c54bb2b91e22 Signed-off-by: Ewout van Bekkum &lt;ewout@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323848 Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323848" owner_email="ewout@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/48/323848/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="Idca946926f5cfd2c87c4a740ad2108010b6b6973" commit="ea3337e48e87d834dcce077efc5f8cfe6b527402" commit_message="vendorcode/google/chromeos/vboot2: honor bot region device size  Vboot keeps track of the size of the hashed region in each RW slot. While that size was being used to calculate the hash it wasn't being honored in restricting the access within the FMAP region for that RW slot. To alleviate that create a sub region that covers the hashed data for the region in which we boot from while performing CBFS accesses.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49764 BUG=chromium:445938 BRANCH=glados TEST=Built and booted chell with cbfstool and dev-util patches.  Change-Id: Idca946926f5cfd2c87c4a740ad2108010b6b6973 Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324093 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324093" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/93/324093/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2015.07" change_id="I1e0cff783f4b072b80589a3a84703a262b86be3a" commit="b536a83c705c06142b6f478e70489a9d936a59ce" commit_message="soc/intel/skylake: unconditionally set SPI controller BAR  The setting of the SPI controller BAR was conditional on the nominal frequency being set. Therefore, that doesn't mean the SPI BAR is set on all boots. Move the setting of the BAR in the southbridge_bootblock_init() which is called prioer to cpu_bootblock_init().  BUG=chrome-os-partner:44827 BRANCH=None TEST=Confirmed spibar is always set on glados.  Change-Id: I1e0cff783f4b072b80589a3a84703a262b86be3a Signed-off-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/319461 Reviewed-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="319461" owner_email="adurbin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/61/319461/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I72bd93a5aaa897d54449a90e3433c1f1dc0db039" commit="acf78603f2169dbc12b903a3a70848b79e37b0fb" commit_message="google-breakpad: switch to new source tree  We've moved the breakpad repo and switch it to the latest upstream tree at the same time.  Update the ebuild to match.  BUG=chromium:579384 TEST=building w/new ebuild passes tests CQ-DEPEND=CL:322990  Change-Id: I72bd93a5aaa897d54449a90e3433c1f1dc0db039 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323010 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dominik Laskowski &lt;domlaskowski@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323010" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/10/323010/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie682aceeb62af98392180d41208a1aa905700651" commit="b606d497856575361d6e1131b17a0ab63b03effd" commit_message="Revert &quot;Revert &quot;drm/nouveau: pmu: Change the init value of elpg_disable_depth to 1&quot;&quot;  This reverts commit 41b5f71a3a131dd25967631d8eb9481d6e692558.  Nouveau ELPG appears to be causing hangs at reboot time.  Disable it for now until the root cause is found.  BUG=b:26544917 TEST=reboot-cycle.sh on Smaug.  Change-Id: Ie682aceeb62af98392180d41208a1aa905700651 Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324085 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324085" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/85/324085/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I64ef50e3400cb5165f22aa12e6c412d869ccf22a" commit="203bac9054ed352c31e20faac75cda4e25e1a8cc" commit_message="faft: Change the spi_voltage config of Celes to pp3300  It makes flashrom able to detect the SPI flash on servo v3.  BUG=None TEST=Manually call host.firmware_install() which sets the spi_voltage value.  Change-Id: I64ef50e3400cb5165f22aa12e6c412d869ccf22a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323824 Commit-Ready: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: danny chan &lt;dchan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323824" owner_email="waihong@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/24/323824/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5151d1a537788aa70b3038f517771861f4d2ddb9" commit="b1158003d8b95b3acae0f170ef999a1b9922cf23" commit_message="Add libdrm to full manifest.  Use chromeos-2.4.66 branch.  BUG=b:26575005 TEST=repo sync, src/third_party/libdrm is there.  Change-Id: I5151d1a537788aa70b3038f517771861f4d2ddb9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323933 Commit-Ready